  "narrative": "The new TP53-loss/USP7 context tests strongly support the central accepted association and justify independent validation of the full-sample claim H48. The signed direction is +1 for TP53 loss versus weaker USP7 dependency, and all four direct context effects are large and precise: adenocarcinoma R40 is +0.803 [0.778, 0.827], Ky library R41 is +0.769 [0.727, 0.812], adherent culture R42 is +0.803 [0.779, 0.827], and MTAP-loss cells R44 is +0.758 [0.709, 0.808]. These are far above any conservative approximate 10% effect benchmark on the dependency-score scale, and the MTAP-loss subgroup lower bound remains very large despite only 69 exposed observations. I therefore accept H51, H52, H53, and H57 as dataset-specific context support and close them as completed robustness checks for H48.\n\nThe MTAP-loss interaction H54 is a useful confounding check but does not support the registered positive interaction. R43 is negative, -0.056 [-0.111, -0.002], indicating a small attenuation of the TP53-loss/weaker-USP7 association in MTAP-loss cells rather than enhancement. Because the main effect remains large within MTAP-loss cells and the interaction magnitude is small relative to the main ~0.76-0.80 effects, I reject H54 as an enhanced MTAP-loss modification claim and close it. Direct MTAP-loss effects on USP7 and MDM2, R45 and R46, are near null and imprecise; H58 and H59 remain unresolved but deferred. They do not show that MTAP loss alone is a dominant driver strong enough to invalidate H48, though correlated 9p co-deletion remains a caution when interpreting this association.\n\nH66 adds a second robustness check for the already independently validated SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 association: within ARID1A-loss cells, SMARCA4 loss remains associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, R47 is +0.805 [0.755, 0.854]. I accept H66 and close it as a completed context check; it does not require separate validation because H12 is already validated.\n\nThe p53-specificity checks are informative. H65 is null/near-null for TP53 loss versus weaker POLR2A dependency: R50 is -0.014 [-0.035, 0.007], and the upper bound is well below a rough clinical benchmark, so I reject the positive POLR2A hypothesis. H67 also does not support the registered stronger DHX9 direction; R51 is negative, -0.024 [-0.044, -0.004], indicating a small opposite direction rather than the claimed association. I reject H67 for the registered hypothesis. Together, these results make the TP53-loss/USP7 association look more selective than a broad p53-loss effect on transcription or helicase dependencies, although residual specificity uncertainty remains.\n\nThe KIF18A tests remain near-null but are not fully conclusive for small clinically meaningful effects: H55 MYC amplification R48 is +0.009 [-0.015, 0.032], and H56 TP53 loss R49 is +0.019 [-0.002, 0.041]. I leave H55 and H56 unresolved and deferred because point estimates are small, intervals include zero, and the upper tails may touch a borderline benchmark; these are low priority relative to H48 validation. Overall, the evidence now supports requesting independent validation for H48. This would test whether the large TP53-loss/weaker-USP7 association is robust beyond the discovery partition and correlated same-dataset structure. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal claims or generalized clinical claims.",
  "research_notes": "Updated validation triage: request independent validation for H48, TP53-loss/weaker-USP7. Context support is now strong: H51 adenocarcinoma R40 +0.803 [0.778,0.827]; H52 Ky R41 +0.769 [0.727,0.812]; H53 adherent R42 +0.803 [0.779,0.827]; H57 MTAP-loss subgroup R44 +0.758 [0.709,0.808]. MTAP interaction H54 rejected for positive interaction (R43 -0.056 [-0.111,-0.002], small attenuation), and direct MTAP effects H58/H59 are near-null deferred; therefore MTAP co-deletion is a caution but not a sufficient reason to defer validation. H66 adds ARID1A-loss context support for already validated H12. H65 rejects TP53-loss weaker POLR2A; H67 rejects registered stronger DHX9 direction, with only small opposite evidence; H48 appears comparatively selective. H55/H56 KIF18A remain unresolved deferred near-null. Next after H48 validation: if H48 validates, consider H13 KEAP1-loss/weaker-NFE2L2 validation; if H48 fails validation, inspect correlated genomic confounding and re-evaluate. Marker D/E/F tests remain lower priority because they are constructed assays without assigned biological role. Maintain that all accepted claims are associations in this supplied dataset/validation split, not causal or generalizable clinical findings."
}

