  "narrative": "The delivered validation resolves both pending deadlines. For H11, MSI-high versus dependency_WRN, the independent validation R26 is +0.797 with lower bound 0.744, while discovery R11 was +0.790 with lower bound 0.760. The direction, magnitude, and practical significance are highly consistent, and both lower bounds are far above any conservative approximate 10% dependency-score benchmark. I therefore keep H11 accepted and close it as an independently replicated dataset-specific association: MSI-high cells show much stronger WRN dependency in this supplied dataset. For H48, TP53 loss versus weaker USP7 dependency, validation R52 is +0.7995 with lower bound 0.768, closely matching discovery R38 +0.804 [0.783,0.825] and the large direct context effects in adenocarcinoma, Ky library, adherent culture, and MTAP-loss cells. I accept H48 and close its investigation as robust within the supplied discovery/validation structure. This is not causal evidence, but it is now one of the strongest supported associations: TP53-loss cells have weaker USP7 dependency. The MTAP-loss checks do not invalidate it: direct MTAP effects were near null, and the MTAP-loss interaction was a small attenuation, not an enhancement, of the TP53 loss effect. The p53 specificity checks also make the USP7 association look relatively selective: TP53 loss was not meaningfully associated with the registered POLR2A hypothesis and did not support the registered stronger DHX9 hypothesis. \n\nThe independently replicated core now includes H11, H12, and H48. The largest remaining unvalidated accepted effect is H13, KEAP1 loss versus weaker NFE2L2 dependency. It is supported by a very large discovery estimate and multiple context-specific confirmations, but it still needs independent validation. I therefore reopened H13 as active and closed the context-specific NFE2L2 confirmations as completed robustness checks. Next analyses should prioritize independent validation of H13, while also running the registered marker modifier tests H17-H23. The new proposals add biologically motivated follow-up: whether STK11 loss modifies the KEAP1/NFE2L2 or MSI/WRN associations, whether ARID1A loss modifies the SMARCA4/SMARCA2 interaction, whether BRCA2 loss increases DHX9 or POLR2A dependency, and whether CDKN2A loss or PTEN loss produce p53- or USP7-related dependency shifts that might indicate broader pathway co-occurrence effects. Negative findings remain important: EGFR amplification failed independent validation for EGFR dependency; KRAS/BRAF/RIT1/ERBB2 contrasts were mostly near null; several MTAP and marker interactions are unresolved but low priority; and constructed markers D/E/F still lack clear interpretation beyond assay controls. All accepted claims remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or guaranteed generalizable clinical claims.",
  "research_notes": "Validated associations now: H11 MSI-high stronger WRN dependency, H12 SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H48 TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency. H48 was newly validated by R52 and is closed; context checks H51/H52/H53/H57 and direct MTAP checks support it, while H54 rejects enhanced MTAP modification. H65/H67 reject broad p53-loss POLR2A/DHX9 directions, so H48 appears selective among tested outcomes. Main next validation target: H13 KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency, currently accepted and reopened active; large discovery and context support but unvalidated. Pending marker modifier tests H17-H23 are useful specificity controls for WRN/SMARCA2/NFE2L2. New registered follow-ups: KEAP1xSTK11 interaction and direct STK11 loss on NFE2L2; MSIxSTK11 interaction on WRN; SMARCA4xARID1A interaction on SMARCA2; BRCA2 loss vs DHX9/POLR2A; CDKN2A loss vs MDM2; PTEN loss vs USP7. Maintain all conclusions as supplied-dataset associations only; no causal or general clinical interpretation."
